<i>Spring will come again</i>

228
00:14:28,435 --> 00:14:30,538
-Come again?
-Spring will come.

229
00:14:30,572 --> 00:14:34,676
When? I haven't seen
a spring or fall since

230
00:14:34,709 --> 00:14:36,611
I can't recall.

231
00:14:36,644 --> 00:14:38,045
That's what I'm working on.

232
00:14:39,279 --> 00:14:41,281
<i>A song to fix</i>
<i>What's wrong</i>

233
00:14:41,315 --> 00:14:43,984
<i>Take what's broken</i>
<i>Make it whole</i>

234
00:14:44,218 --> 00:14:46,453
<i>A song so beautiful</i>

235
00:14:46,487 --> 00:14:50,558
<i>It brings the world</i>
<i>Back into tune</i>

236
00:14:50,592 --> 00:14:52,527
<i>Back into time</i>

237
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:56,096
<i>And all the flowers will bloom</i>

238
00:14:56,130 --> 00:14:59,433
-When you become my wife.
-Oh, he's crazy.

239
00:15:00,668 --> 00:15:03,170
Why would I become his wife?

240
00:15:03,203 --> 00:15:07,542
Maybe because he'll
make you feel alive.

241
00:15:08,375 --> 00:15:10,144
Alive...

242
00:15:11,378 --> 00:15:12,946
That's worth a lot.

243
00:15:15,182 --> 00:15:16,316
What else you got?

244
00:15:27,762 --> 00:15:30,632
<i>Lover, tell me</i>
<i>If you can</i>

245
00:15:30,665 --> 00:15:33,267
<i>Who's gonna buy</i>
<i>the wedding bands?</i>

246
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:35,703
<i>Times being what they are</i>

247
00:15:35,737 --> 00:15:38,606
<i>Hot and getting hotter</i>
<i>All the time</i>

248
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:41,175
<i>Lover, when I</i>
<i>Sing my song</i>

249
00:15:41,208 --> 00:15:43,477
<i>All the rivers will sing along</i>

250
00:15:43,511 --> 00:15:46,313
<i>And they're gonna break</i>
<i>Their banks for us</i>

251
00:15:46,346 --> 00:15:48,750
<i>And with their gold</i>
<i>Be generous</i>

252
00:15:48,783 --> 00:15:51,586
<i>All a-flashing in the pan</i>

253
00:15:51,619 --> 00:15:54,188
<i>All to fashion for your hand</i>

254
00:15:54,221 --> 00:15:58,025
<i>The river's gonna give us</i>
<i>The wedding bands</i>

255
00:16:02,095 --> 00:16:04,699
<i>Lover, tell me</i>
<i>If you're able</i>

256
00:16:04,732 --> 00:16:07,234
<i>Who's gonna lay</i>
<i>The wedding table?</i>

257
00:16:07,267 --> 00:16:09,771
<i>Times being what they are</i>

258
00:16:09,804 --> 00:16:12,540
<i>Dark and getting</i>
<i>Darker all the time</i>

259
00:16:12,574 --> 00:16:15,042
<i>Lover, when I sing my song</i>

260
00:16:15,075 --> 00:16:17,411
<i>All the trees</i>
<i>Gonna sing along</i>

261
00:16:17,444 --> 00:16:20,247
<i>And they're gonna bend</i>
<i>Their branches down</i>

262
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:22,617
<i>To lay their fruit</i>
<i>Upon the ground</i>

263
00:16:22,650 --> 00:16:25,052
<i>The almond and the apple</i>

264
00:16:25,085 --> 00:16:27,454
<i>And the sugar from the maple</i>

265
00:16:27,655 --> 00:16:31,726
<i>The trees gonna lay</i>
<i>The wedding table</i>

266
00:16:49,777 --> 00:16:52,246
So when you sing your song.

267
00:16:52,279 --> 00:16:54,481
The one you're working on.

268
00:16:54,516 --> 00:16:56,618
Spring will come again.

269
00:16:57,451 --> 00:16:59,787
-Yes.
-Why don't you sing it, then?

270
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:02,222
It isn't finished.

271
00:17:02,690 --> 00:17:03,758
Sing it!

272
00:17:05,392 --> 00:17:07,160
You want to take me home?

273
00:17:07,194 --> 00:17:09,162
-Yes.
-Sing the song.

274
00:17:20,742 --> 00:17:26,681
<i>Laaa la la la la la laaa</i>

275
00:17:28,650 --> 00:17:31,553
<i>Laaa la la la la la laaa</i>

276
00:17:31,586 --> 00:17:37,491
<i>-Laaa la la la la laaa</i>
<i>-Laaa la la la la laaa</i>

277
00:17:37,525 --> 00:17:41,395
<i>Laaa la la la la la laaa</i>

278
00:17:41,428 --> 00:17:45,098
<i>La la la laaa laaa laaa</i>

279
00:17:45,132 --> 00:17:50,605
<i>Laaa la la la la laaa</i>

280
00:17:53,140 --> 00:17:55,409
-How'd you do that?
-I don't know.

281
00:17:56,410 --> 00:17:58,312
The song's not finished, though.

282
00:17:58,580 --> 00:18:00,615
Even so, it can do this.

283
00:18:01,248 --> 00:18:02,282
I know.

284
00:18:02,316 --> 00:18:03,818
You have to finish it.

285
00:18:05,853 --> 00:18:08,623
<i>Lover, tell me</i>
<i>When we're wed</i>

286
00:18:08,656 --> 00:18:11,291
<i>Who's gonna make</i>
<i>The wedding bed?</i>

287
00:18:11,325 --> 00:18:13,761
<i>Times being what they are</i>

288
00:18:13,795 --> 00:18:16,631
<i>Hot and getting hotter</i>
<i>All the time</i>

289
00:18:16,664 --> 00:18:18,900
<i>Lover, when I</i>
<i>Sing my song</i>

290
00:18:18,933 --> 00:18:21,468
<i>All the birds</i>
<i>Gonna sing along</i>

291
00:18:21,502 --> 00:18:24,304
<i>And they'll come flying</i>
<i>From all around</i>

292
00:18:24,338 --> 00:18:26,808
<i>To lay their feathers</i>
<i>On the ground</i>

293
00:18:26,841 --> 00:18:29,744
<i>And we'll lie down</i>
<i>In eiderdown</i>

294
00:18:29,777 --> 00:18:31,613
<i>A pillow 'neath our heads</i>

295
00:18:31,913 --> 00:18:36,249
<i>The birds gonna make</i>
<i>The wedding bed</i>

296
00:18:36,851 --> 00:18:41,889
<i>And the trees gonna lay</i>
<i>The wedding table</i>

297
00:18:42,389 --> 00:18:46,761
<i>And the river's gonna give</i>
<i>Us the wedding bands</i>

298
00:18:47,795 --> 00:18:54,802
<i>-Mmmm</i>
<i>-Mmmm</i>

299
00:18:57,772 --> 00:19:00,307
[audience cheering]

300
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:14,589
Where'd you get that melody?

301
00:19:15,623 --> 00:19:18,225
<i>I don't know</i>
<i>It came to me</i>

302
00:19:18,258 --> 00:19:20,293
<i>As if I'd known it all along</i>

303
00:19:20,327 --> 00:19:21,428
You have.

304
00:19:21,461 --> 00:19:23,698
<i>It's an old song</i>

305
00:19:23,898 --> 00:19:26,934
<i>A song of love</i>
<i>From long ago</i>

306
00:19:26,968 --> 00:19:29,804
<i>Long time since</i>
<i>I heard it, though</i>

307
00:19:29,837 --> 00:19:31,806
You've heard that melody before?

308
00:19:31,839 --> 00:19:34,274
-Sure.
-Tell me more.

309
00:19:34,809 --> 00:19:38,880
Remember the tale I told you
once about the gods?

310
00:19:38,913 --> 00:19:41,949
-Which ones?
-Hades and Persephone.

311
00:19:41,983 --> 00:19:44,484
Remember how it used to be.

312
00:19:44,519 --> 00:19:48,589
Their love that made
the world go round.

313
00:19:48,623 --> 00:19:53,928
Yeah, I remember now.
But that was long ago.

314
00:19:53,961 --> 00:19:56,229
Tell it again, though.

315
00:20:06,741 --> 00:20:08,810
[audience giggles]

316
00:20:12,312 --> 00:20:14,515
<i>King of shadows</i>

317
00:20:16,851 --> 00:20:19,319
<i>King of shades</i>

318
00:20:19,954 --> 00:20:25,827
<i>Hades was King</i>
<i>Of the Underworld</i>

319
00:20:29,931 --> 00:20:36,236
<i>But he fell in love</i>
<i>With a beautiful lady</i>

320
00:20:36,838 --> 00:20:41,876
<i>Who walked up above</i>
<i>In her mother's green field</i>

321
00:20:43,878 --> 00:20:48,649
<i>He fell in love</i>
<i>With Persephone</i>

322
00:20:49,016 --> 00:20:52,687
<i>Who was gathering flowers</i>
<i>In the light of the sun</i>

323
00:20:54,989 --> 00:20:59,292
<i>And he took her home</i>
<i>To become his queen</i>

324
00:21:01,062 --> 00:21:04,498
<i>Where the sun never shone</i>

325
00:21:04,532 --> 00:21:07,467
<i>On anyone</i>

326
00:21:09,637 --> 00:21:10,772
Go on.

327
00:21:12,774 --> 00:21:18,311
<i>The lady loved him</i>
<i>And the kingdom they shared</i>

328
00:21:20,982 --> 00:21:25,686
<i>But without her above</i>
<i>Not one flower would grow</i>

329
00:21:26,854 --> 00:21:33,594
<i>So King Hades agreed</i>
<i>That for half of each year</i>

330
00:21:33,628 --> 00:21:36,296
<i>She would stay</i>
<i>With him there</i>

331
00:21:36,631 --> 00:21:39,332
<i>In his world down below</i>

332
00:21:42,036 --> 00:21:45,807
<i>But the other half</i>
<i>She could walk in the sun</i>

333
00:21:47,775 --> 00:21:52,013
<i>And the sun in turn</i>
<i>Burned twice as bright</i>

334
00:21:54,115 --> 00:21:58,686
<i>Which is where</i>
<i>The seasons come from</i>

335
00:21:58,719 --> 00:22:04,759
<i>And with them the cycle</i>
<i>Of the seed and the sickle</i>

336
00:22:04,792 --> 00:22:07,460
<i>And the lives of the people</i>

337
00:22:07,795 --> 00:22:11,732
<i>And the birds in their flight</i>

338
00:22:11,766 --> 00:22:13,500
Singing...

339
00:22:15,970 --> 00:22:20,007
<i>Laaa la la la la la laaa</i>

340
00:22:20,041 --> 00:22:23,811
Down below and up above.

341
00:22:23,845 --> 00:22:27,882
<i>Laaa la la la la la laaa</i>

342
00:22:27,915 --> 00:22:30,818
In harmony and rhythm.

343
00:22:31,786 --> 00:22:38,491
<i>-Laaa la la la la la laaa</i>
-The gods sang a song of love

344
00:22:39,627 --> 00:22:43,764
<i>Laaa la la la la la</i>

345
00:22:43,798 --> 00:22:46,701
and the world sang it with them.

346
00:22:47,101 --> 00:22:49,737
<i>But that was long ago</i>

347
00:22:49,770 --> 00:22:53,608
<i>Before we were on this road</i>

348
00:22:58,579 --> 00:23:01,616
<i>And on the road to hell</i>
<i>There was a lot of waiting</i>

349
00:23:01,649 --> 00:23:03,551
<i>Mmmm, waiting</i>

350
00:23:03,851 --> 00:23:06,419
<i>Everybody waiting on a train</i>

351
00:23:06,453 --> 00:23:08,789
<i>Mmmm, waiting on the lady</i>
<i>With the--</i>

352
00:23:08,823 --> 00:23:11,192
<i>Waiting on the train</i>
<i>To bring that lady</i>

353
00:23:11,225 --> 00:23:12,927
<i>Mmmm, lady!</i>

354
00:23:12,960 --> 00:23:15,830
<i>With the suitcase back again</i>

355
00:23:16,697 --> 00:23:18,699
<i>She's never early always late</i>

356
00:23:18,733 --> 00:23:20,101
<i>Waiting, waiting</i>

357
00:23:20,134 --> 00:23:23,004
<i>These days she never</i>
<i>Stays for long</i>

358
00:23:23,037 --> 00:23:25,072
<i>But good things come</i>
<i>To those who wait</i>

359
00:23:25,106 --> 00:23:27,775
<i>Mmmm</i>

360
00:23:27,808 --> 00:23:30,177
[train whistle toots]

361
00:23:30,912 --> 00:23:32,479
Here she comes!

362
00:23:32,513 --> 00:23:34,882
<i>Well, it's like he said</i>
<i>I'm an outdoor girl</i>

363
00:23:34,916 --> 00:23:37,450
And you're late again.

364
00:23:37,484 --> 00:23:39,854
<i>Married to the King</i>
<i>Of the Underworld</i>

365
00:23:39,887 --> 00:23:42,523
She forgot a little thing
called "spring."

366
00:23:42,556 --> 00:23:44,926
<i>Are you wondering</i>
<i>Where I've been?</i>

367
00:23:44,959 --> 00:23:46,193
-Yeah!
-Where you been?

368
00:23:46,227 --> 00:23:47,094
I'm wondering.

369
00:23:47,128 --> 00:23:49,664
<i>Been to hell</i>
<i>And back again</i>

370
00:23:49,697 --> 00:23:51,766
<i>But like my mama</i>
<i>Always said</i>

371
00:23:51,799 --> 00:23:54,135
<i>Brother, when you're down</i>
<i>You're down</i>

372
00:23:54,168 --> 00:23:56,037
<i>And when you're up</i>
<i>You're up</i>

373
00:23:56,637 --> 00:23:58,906
<i>If you ain't six feet</i>
<i>Underground</i>

374
00:23:58,940 --> 00:24:00,908
<i>You're living it up on top</i>

375
00:24:00,942 --> 00:24:03,644
<i>Let's not talk</i>
<i>About hard times</i>

376
00:24:03,678 --> 00:24:06,047
<i>Pour the wine</i>
<i>It's summertime</i>

377
00:24:06,080 --> 00:24:07,682
<i>'Cos right now</i>
<i>We're living it</i>

378
00:24:07,715 --> 00:24:10,483
<i>-How are we livin' it?</i>
<i>-Livin' it, livin' it up</i>

379
00:24:10,518 --> 00:24:12,019
<i>Oh, brother, right here</i>
<i>We're livin' it</i>

380
00:24:12,053 --> 00:24:15,089
<i>-Where are we livin' it?</i>
<i>-Livin' it up on top</i>

381
00:24:15,957 --> 00:24:18,159
Who makes the summer sun
shine bright?

382
00:24:18,192 --> 00:24:20,493
That's right, Persephone!

383
00:24:20,861 --> 00:24:22,830
<i>Who makes the fruit</i>
<i>Of the vine get ripe?</i>

384
00:24:22,863 --> 00:24:25,199
<i>-Persephone!</i>
<i>-That's me!</i>

385
00:24:25,232 --> 00:24:28,769
<i>Who makes the flowers bloom</i>
<i>Again in spite of her man</i>

386
00:24:28,803 --> 00:24:30,071
<i>You do!</i>

387
00:24:30,838 --> 00:24:32,606
<i>Who is doing</i>
<i>The best she can?</i>

388
00:24:32,640 --> 00:24:34,909
Persephone, that's who.

389
00:24:34,942 --> 00:24:39,213
<i>Now, some may say the weather</i>
<i>Ain't the way it used to be</i>

390
00:24:39,947 --> 00:24:44,618
<i>But let me tell you something</i>
<i>That my mama said to me</i>

391
00:24:44,652 --> 00:24:48,756
<i>You take what you can get</i>
<i>And you make the most of it</i>

392
00:24:48,789 --> 00:24:51,792
<i>-So right now we're livin' in</i>
<i>-How are we livin' it?</i>

393
00:24:51,826 --> 00:24:54,795
<i>Livin' it, livin' it up</i>
<i>Oh, brother, right here</i>

394
00:24:54,829 --> 00:24:56,831
<i>-we're livin' it</i>
<i>-Where are we livin' it?</i>

395
00:24:56,864 --> 00:24:58,666
<i>Livin' it up on top</i>

396
00:24:58,899 --> 00:25:02,036
It was summertime
on the road to hell.

397
00:25:02,069 --> 00:25:03,604
<i>Mmmm</i>

398
00:25:03,637 --> 00:25:06,540
There was a girl
who had always run away.

399
00:25:06,574 --> 00:25:08,275
<i>Mmmm</i>

400
00:25:08,309 --> 00:25:12,213
You might say that it was
in spite of herself.

401
00:25:12,246 --> 00:25:13,547
<i>Mmmm, Mmmm, Mmmm</i>

402
00:25:13,581 --> 00:25:16,017
That this young girl
decided to stay.

403
00:25:16,350 --> 00:25:18,719
<i>There was a poor boy</i>
<i>With a lyre</i>

404
00:25:18,753 --> 00:25:20,821
Who says times are hard?

405
00:25:20,855 --> 00:25:22,890
Flowers bloom,
the fruit got ripe.

406
00:25:22,923 --> 00:25:25,092
And brother, for a moment there.

407
00:25:25,126 --> 00:25:27,161
Anybody want a drink?

408
00:25:27,695 --> 00:25:31,198
the world came back to life.

409
00:25:31,232 --> 00:25:32,733
Ooh!

410
00:25:33,601 --> 00:25:34,268
Hey.

411
00:25:35,870 --> 00:25:38,873
[Chorus cheering]

412
00:25:40,841 --> 00:25:42,610
-Hey!
-Hey!

413
00:25:42,643 --> 00:25:43,611
-Hey!
-Ho!

414
00:25:43,644 --> 00:25:45,613
-Hey!
-Ho!

415
00:25:47,348 --> 00:25:48,816
Come on, now!

416
00:25:50,084 --> 00:25:51,052
Whoo!

417
00:25:55,923 --> 00:25:57,958
Hey, hey. Hey!

418
00:26:05,366 --> 00:26:08,069
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

419
00:26:09,837 --> 00:26:12,073
[audience cheering]

420
00:26:17,912 --> 00:26:20,314
[audience clapping to the beat]

421
00:26:52,179 --> 00:26:54,748
<i>Up on top</i>
<i>We ain't got much</i>

422
00:26:54,782 --> 00:26:57,017
<i>But we're livin' it</i>
<i>Livin' it up</i>

423
00:26:57,351 --> 00:26:59,386
<i>Just enough to fill our cups</i>

424
00:27:00,054 --> 00:27:01,922
<i>Livin it up on top</i>

425
00:27:01,956 --> 00:27:04,425
<i>Brother,</i>
<i>Pass that bottle around</i>

426
00:27:04,458 --> 00:27:06,694
<i>'Cos we're livin' it</i>
<i>Livin' it up</i>

427
00:27:06,727 --> 00:27:08,829
Let the poet bless this round.

428
00:27:08,863 --> 00:27:09,830
Yeah!

429
00:27:09,864 --> 00:27:11,866
-Orpheus!
-Orpheus.

430
00:27:14,368 --> 00:27:17,238
<i>To the patroness</i>
<i>Of all of this</i>

431
00:27:17,271 --> 00:27:18,706
Persephone!

432
00:27:18,739 --> 00:27:20,341
-Hear, hear!
-Hear, hear!

433
00:27:20,374 --> 00:27:24,778
<i>Who's finally returned to us</i>
<i>With wine enough to share</i>

434
00:27:24,812 --> 00:27:25,713
Uh-huh!

435
00:27:25,746 --> 00:27:27,381
<i>Asking nothing in return</i>

436
00:27:28,716 --> 00:27:30,151
<i>'Cept that we should live</i>

437
00:27:30,184 --> 00:27:33,721
<i>And learn to live as</i>
<i>Brothers in this life</i>

438
00:27:34,788 --> 00:27:36,724
<i>And to trust</i>
<i>She will provide</i>

439
00:27:36,757 --> 00:27:37,424
Alright.

440
00:27:38,792 --> 00:27:40,928
And if no one
takes too much.

441
00:27:40,961 --> 00:27:42,897
There will always be enough.

442
00:27:44,198 --> 00:27:47,334
-She will always fill our cups.
-I will!

443
00:27:47,368 --> 00:27:48,903
And we will always

444
00:27:52,239 --> 00:27:53,774
raise 'em up.

445
00:28:00,447 --> 00:28:03,017
To the world we dream about...

446
00:28:04,752 --> 00:28:05,719
and...

447
00:28:10,991 --> 00:28:12,960
the one we live in now.

